WEBVTT

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.470
Hey, Ren. Breakfast is ready.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.750
I'll eat once I get changed.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.480
Are you okay with plum and 
shiso rolls for lunch today?

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.250
They're my favorite.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.930
Want me to add a cold pack to your lunch?

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:30.750
Yeah, thanks.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.100
Why aren't you wearing anything?!

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.760
Unashamed

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.760
I forgot to bring a change of clothes.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.390
Ren, you...

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.140
Don't ever let anyone but me see you like that.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.620
So if it's just you, it's okay?

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.400
Yes!

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:50.940
This lecture is making it really clear 
what his underlying motives are.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.400
If anything, it's underscoring his
perversion so much that I could cry.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.900
You need to at least wear underwear!

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.030
Shut up.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.100
Kaidou. Kaidou Ren.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.120
What is it?

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.760
Today was your third lecture 
with an outside teacher.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.260
How'd it go? Did you enjoy it?

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.260
I think it was worthwhile.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.500
Today, the professor and I discussed practical

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.080
implementation of microprocessors 
that use algorithms to—

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.270
Stop right there.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.270
I may be your homeroom teacher, 
but I'm a simple PE teacher.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.520
Then why did you ask?

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.800
Yes, that! That's it!

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.580
There's nothing lovable about you.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.360
The vice principal, who attended the lecture 
with you, took stomach medicine earlier.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.030
Why?

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.480
Because you're dealing with a college professor,

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.630
yet you show no respect, 
respond curtly, and never smile.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.180
Is that a problem?

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.610
Kaidou, do you intend to keep living in Japan?

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.820
And attend college here?

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.700
That's the idea. I don't have plans to leave Japan.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.550
I see.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.440
I read your essay the other day.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.850
It was awful.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.320
Even kindergarteners these days
can write better than that.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.310
You lack emotion.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.540
You're an honest and good student, 
but you're still an idiot.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.210
The only one in your class you
can talk to is Kurosaki Juuzen.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.580
Well, he's a real idiot, though.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.820
There are different types of idiots?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.190
In any case, I've spoken with the vice principal,

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.440
and we're putting your special lectures on hold.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.080
You need to learn your 
classmates' names and faces.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.080
And polite Japanese. And how to smile.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:53.910
Got it?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.320
Haru-chan, you're so good with children.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.540
Is it because you have three younger brothers?

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.260
You think so? My family's all boys.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.720
I wish I'd had at least one sister.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.120
Girls are just different, you know?

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.780
Oh, Ren Ren? Welcome home.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.480
Come on in. Haru-san's going on break soon.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.090
Ren?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.670
Haru.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:22.500
Welcome home.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.450
You must be thirsty. 
Want something to drink?

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.020
Anything is fine.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.950
I see. Then go in the back and wait for me.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:35.330
Good grief. Haven't they noticed 
that more and more customers

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.980
stick around until this hour just to see this?

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.090
So cute!

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.090
So cute!

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:45.590
Here, Ren. I've got iced tea, 
a black tea muffin, and a banana muffin.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:46.950
Which do you want?

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.360
Either's fine.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.720
Then we'll split both.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.990
Haru, sorry I'm not your sister.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.110
What? Were you listening earlier?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.860
I just happened to hear you.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.310
I meant if I had another sibling.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:10.490
If you were a girl, I'd be so worried, 
I wouldn't be able to sleep at night.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.410
I don't need your concern, 
whether I'm a boy or a girl.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:19.130
Really? You seem awfully grumpy.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.890
Did something happen at school, Ren?

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:23.600
Nothing.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.540
Really?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.050
Nothing to say.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.130
Uh-oh.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.860
You can't say it in Japanese? Is it too hard?

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:33.630
My listening and reading are mostly fine.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.140
I guess I can see that.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.080
Japanese isn't Haruko-san's 
native tongue, either.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:42.730
Haruko speaks three other languages, 
in addition to Japanese and English.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:46.150
That environment may not 
have been good for you.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.100
What did you do, Haru?

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.830
Well, in my case,

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:53.340
the girls in my class taught 
me all sorts of things...

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.660
Ow, ow, ow! I was joking!

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.680
<i>It's true, though.</i>

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.730
Since you grew up in a unique 
environment, maybe you can't help it.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.210
You'll get used to it in time.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>In Ren's case, that's not the problem.</i>

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.990
<i>Ren's emotions are simple.</i>

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.850
<i>They're just underdeveloped, really,</i>

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.690
<i>and haven't branched out 
into more complex feelings.</i>

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.890
<i>Normally, he's expressionless, 
but he doesn't hide how he feels.</i>

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.270
<i>In some ways, it makes him easy to read.</i>

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.480
What is it?

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.410
Look at all these wrinkles in your brow.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:30.970
Rub Rub

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.310
You're going to ruin your cute face.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.410
I don't care. You're just too flippant.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.290
Really?

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:40.500
I'm just happy every day because 
I get to live with the Ren I love.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.360
Come on, Ren, come over here.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.420
Is there anything I can do?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.250
Yes.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:49.930
What you want to do after this.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.540
Got it.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.890
<i>Oh, damn.</i>

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.810
<i>This feels seriously good.</i>

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:03.460
<i>Come to think of it, does he 
have any sexual desire?</i>

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.300
<i>I thought he was still just a kid.</i>

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:11.890
<i>Now that I think about it, maybe sleeping 
with him every night isn't... good...</i>

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.290
Ren, my field of vision is red.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:25.170
Dribble

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.870
Are you okay?

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.850
I'm fine. You're the one who's not okay.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.170
You piece of shit,

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:28.050
what are you doing in here?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:31.680
You've got guts, to sexually harass someone 
while working us like slaves for free.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.870
Get back to work!

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.930
He's in a bad mood.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.680
Aki's mad whenever he's not in a good mood.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.940
Fine, then. Break time is over.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.300
What is it?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.470
That's why Aki's so angry.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.280
Shima?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.920
Who's that with him?

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:01.290
A student Shima is tutoring, Natsukawa Ai-chan.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.820
She's totally smitten with him.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:04.970
Oh. Are they dating?

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:08.660
What? Of course not. She's in middle school.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.300
Their grandmothers are friends.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:16.470
Though, apparently, she isn't 
attending school right now.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.300
Why not?

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:21.640
Her parents divorced last year, and she 
wasn't getting along with her classmates.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.480
She seemed to have a lot going on...

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.670
But that's not unusual, I guess.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:33.770
<i>Does she seem so happy despite all that
because Shima is sitting next to her?</i>

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.010
Are you stupid?!

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:45.810
What time do you think it is? 
You're a real idiot if you go out to see her!

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.810
This is why I told you to quit tutoring!

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:53.090
I'm still responsible for her. 
I can't just ignore her.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.970
Why? She takes advantage of you 
because you baby her all the time!

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.440
She has no one else to turn to now.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:03.480
You and I know how lonely
it can be with no parents.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.740
That goes for Ren, too,

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:08.730
but has he ever caused 
this much trouble for anyone?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:12.420
Hey, guys. Don't be so loud 
in the middle of the night.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.950
If you want to shout, 
do it somewhere else.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:16.390
Bro... But he's...

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.010
Sorry for waking you, Brother.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.740
Can I go out for a little bit?

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:20.700
Shima!

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:21.870
Is it urgent?

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.590
The Natsukawa girl ran away from home.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.950
She's right outside now.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:31.160
I see. If that's the case, Aki, 
quit yelling. You're too loud.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.360
I'll be back. Don't wait up for me.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:35.380
Be careful.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:01.150
Shima.

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:06.640
Ren...

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.170
You shouldn't sleep out here.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.450
You'll catch a cold.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.370
Aki would've yelled if I'd gone 
into our room, so I slept here.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:14.510
What time is it?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.260
Four.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:19.260
Ren, were you out running 
this early in the morning?

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:23.260
It's cool in the morning, and there 
are too many people in the evening.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.270
Why don't you take a break today?

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:31.070
You couldn't have gotten much 
sleep with us shouting last night.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:34.270
It's no big deal. Getting out of 
shape would be a bigger problem.

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:40.030
If you strain your body too hard while 
you're growing, you won't get any taller.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.270
I'm going to bed.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:46.040
That's right. Sleep is important.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.290
Shima.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:53.570
Does being a tutor require you to be so kind?

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.180
Enough to go out when called 
in the middle of the night?

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.890
Oh, you mean Ai-chan?

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.300
I imagine things are different, normally.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.700
But for certain reasons,

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.960
she's living with her grandmother 
instead of her parents.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:07.950
Because of that, she hasn't 
been doing very well at school.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:13.030
Since her situation is similar to mine, 
I understand how she feels.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.820
I can't ignore her.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.070
No.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:20.400
She's more like Aki than like you.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.800
They feel similar.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.700
Isn't that why you can't ignore her?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:32.780
<i>I can see why our brother 
can't resist this younger boy.</i>

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.700
Shima, you're just like Haru.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.750
You think things that 
don't matter are important.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.320
It's a bad habit.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.710
<i>And he hits you where it hurts.</i>

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.350
Hey, Kaidou.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:52.140
Have you learned the names 
and faces of everyone in your class?

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.950
I memorized all their names 
in alphabetical order.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:55.810
What about their faces?

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.150
I have trouble telling Japanese people apart.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:01.070
Well, I wasn't expecting much.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.150
Now smile!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:07.740
Creak...

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:06.710
Hey, teach, what are you doing to Ren?

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:07.740
Smiling practice.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.250
Don't you think that's too hard for him?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.370
If I don't teach this awkward kid 
how to at least force a smile,

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:15.900
he'll keep making me uneasy.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:19.800
Well, yeah. I'd like to see Ren 
laughing like an idiot, too.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:20.760
Hey, try laughing.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:25.760
Creak...

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.600
What the hell is that face?

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.880
I can hear your face creaking!

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.820
Kurosaki, you don't need to be that harsh.

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.020
Huh?

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.180
Ren, you're alone? Where's Brother?

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:40.030
He and Aki were called to the café.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.400
Isn't it Kiyoka-san's bar starting at six?

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:48.410
Some café regulars are at the bar and 
said they wanted to eat Haru's cooking.

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:50.410
Do you want dinner?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.430
Yeah.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:53.750
Give me a minute. I'll reheat it.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.870
Thanks. I'll put my things away.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:01.840
Hey, Ren.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.090
Who taught you how to use chopsticks?

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.530
Your brother.

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:13.000
I thought so. You hold 
your chopsticks like he does.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:14.850
You eat just like him, too.

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:17.570
It's not just chopsticks.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.560
He taught me how to use a knife and fork,

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.610
how to greet people in 
the morning and evening,

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.860
what to say before and after meals...

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.440
To eat three meals a day.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.990
To sleep in a bed at night.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:37.000
To tell someone if I feel hurt, 
sick, or unhappy about something.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:42.330
To always clearly say "thank you" and "I'm sorry."

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:47.360
In just a single summer, 
Haru taught me all those things.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.480
Both pleasant and unpleasant things.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.180
Haru taught me everything.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.370
<i>This kid really is...</i>

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:03.200
Shima.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.440
I'm borrowing your study materials.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.030
Okay. Are you done working?

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:09.990
Yeah.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:14.290
Sheesh... They should've gone 
somewhere nicer for their anniversary.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:18.760
They just came as a couple to see Bro's face.

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.610
People seem to have figured out 
that he used to be a host.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:24.800
At this rate, there's no telling when 
his former customers will start coming.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:25.530
Yeah.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:26.880
And he's not blameless, either.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.260
If it bothers him, he should say no.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.510
He wouldn't be him if he could do that.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:34.560
I know. I'm borrowing this, okay?

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.240
Aki.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:35.770
What?

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.770
I'm not quitting my tutoring job.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:44.600
Is that so? Do what you want, then. 
It's not my problem.

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:45.420
But...

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:50.360
If she asks me out again, 
I won't go to meet her.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.370
Is that okay?

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.320
That's fine.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.460
I worked so hard today.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.940
Ren, put more of your weight into it.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:06.150
I am.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.510
Sorry I couldn't eat dinner with you today.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.470
If you have work, you can't help it.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:15.260
Besides, Shima came home, 
so I didn't eat alone.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:17.350
Really? Shima, huh?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.020
Is something funny?

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:24.630
Nah, I was just wondering what you 
two talked about while you ate.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:28.020
Normal stuff. But we mostly talked about you.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:32.030
What?! You better not have 
been talking trash about me!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.490
We talked about who taught 
me how to use chopsticks.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:36.740
Chopsticks?

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:39.710
He said I hold them like you do.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.020
Oh, right.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:45.810
I was the one who taught you, since you 
tried to eat everything with your hands.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:49.800
I told him there were a lot of 
other things you taught me, too.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.970
By the end, I tired you out, 
and you'd actually listen to me.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:57.370
You were really persistent.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.980
Don't make that face as you remember it...

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:04.730
I can't believe how much that 
impudent little brat has grown.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:07.270
Sorry for being an impudent brat.

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:12.780
But you were super cute then, 
and you're still cute now.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.740
Besides, when I look at you now,

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:20.460
I know my efforts weren't wasted.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.370
Ren, what's wrong?

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:30.440
You always smile so easily.

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:33.070
I don't understand how you can be so happy.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.540
It's something I just can't copy.

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:39.070
You don't need to force yourself to smile.

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:42.640
What's wrong?

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.200
Ren?

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:49.710
<i>Haru has never told me to smile.</i>

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:50.600
Haru...

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:54.390
<i>Aki and Shima have never 
told me to smile, either.</i>

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.880
<i>It's because they know.</i>

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.300
You must've been straining yourself.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.660
<i>I'm sorry I didn't notice...</i>

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.670
What's with the surprise attack?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:12.690
...that forcing yourself to smile is so painful.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:12.690
<i>...that forcing yourself to smile is so painful.</i>

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.600
<i>Haru was always smiling.</i>

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.770
<i>He'd get mad sometimes,</i>

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:23.080
<i>but afterwards he'd always show me a smile.</i>

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:27.410
<i>As a child, I found it mysterious.</i>

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:32.010
<i>I felt like I was constantly 
looking at Haru's face.</i>

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:36.340
<i>He did it for me...</i>

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.620
<i>For a child who didn't know how to smile.</i>

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:44.330
Huh?

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:48.530
Wh-What are you doing?

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:50.380
Let me join you.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.670
Where's Ren?

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.170
He's asleep.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.920
Isn't the café open tomorrow? 
You should sleep, too.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:58.770
I can't tonight! Not tonight!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:01.180
You're oozing adrenaline.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.880
I did something really uncool 
in front of Ren today.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:06.170
"Today"? You mean "again."

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:09.310
What? No way! Ren doesn't say I'm cool?

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:12.190
I've never heard Ren say that.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.900
In any case, today was especially bad. 
He caught me off-guard.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.700
What? Did he finally jump you?

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:21.580
Wha— Shima, how can you say that?!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.700
Well, he is pretty masculine. It could happen.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.300
That's right! He actually made me cry!

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:32.340
That must've been a miserable sight to behold.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.190
Don't call me miserable!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.720
It's no use. I...

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.480
I love him!

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.820
You're just now realizing this?

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:43.740
<i>I was so arrogant.</i>

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.430
<i>I thought I would always be
the one showing affection.</i>

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:49.040
<i>But he turned that on its head</i>

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:53.360
<i>and got me when my defenses were down.</i>

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.810
<i>I don't need to worry.</i>

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:12.090
<i>Ren will smile someday, 
like a blooming flower.</i>

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.630
I told you...

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:21.470
Normally, when this happens, 
you apologize to your superiors.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.910
When you bump into someone, 
you can't just say, "My bad!"

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:26.570
That'll just get you punched!

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:29.100
It doesn't help me when you say

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:32.220
that something is normal,
or it's what everyone does.

00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:37.150
I don't understand what's 
normal for Japanese people.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.620
<i>I need to start there?</i>

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:40.490
This is going to take a long time.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.720
It's impossible, teach.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:46.040
Those are just bad habits 
that Japanese people have.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.640
You can't force Kaidou to act that way. Right?

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:52.790
It'd be like telling me to fix my accent.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.490
You guys understand his Japanese? 
You know what he's saying?

00:19:58.490 --> 00:19:59.730
We're totally fine.

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:03.870
Kaidou's Japanese is better 
than ours. It's more correct.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:06.250
He speaks like a middle-aged man.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.450
I don't understand young people these days.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.020
Ren!

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.460
Could you translate this English for me?

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.020
I'm gonna be asked to read it today.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.740
If you'll write my journal entry for today.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:22.030
I can't. I don't have your literary talent.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.570
Then do it yourself.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.510
Hey, Ren. Let me tell you something special.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:32.680
The essay you wrote the other day 
was posted in front of the faculty office.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:35.870
What? That old fart!

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:39.040
I think your Japanese is just fine.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:46.800
Um, will Shima-sensei be much longer?

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.060
Shima's running late.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.180
Are you unhappy with having me here until then?

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.500
We look the same, anyway.

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.560
Huh? Oh, I didn't mean that!

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:59.730
B-Besides, you and Shima-sensei may 
be twins, but you're nothing alike.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.010
You have the same face,

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:04.050
but you're different sizes and have 
different personalities. It's strange.

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:10.540
Today, I just wanted to tell 
Shima-sensei in person that

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:09.750
Welcome home.

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:10.540
Thanks.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.830
I'm going to start attending school next week.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:13.920
Oh?

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:18.660
And I wanted to thank him for 
walking me home the other day.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.840
My grandparents were furious 
with me after that.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:26.190
They said Shima-sensei's home life 
is very complicated and difficult.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:30.050
I'd heard your parents had passed away,

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:33.350
but I didn't know the details.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:36.710
I wouldn't call it complicated.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:40.700
We just have a half-brother and 
another we're not related to at all.

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:43.920
Really? But the four of you seem so similar.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.110
Similar? The four of us?

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.390
Aren't you brothers? You feel alike.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:57.440
Especially your oldest and youngest brothers.

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:40.300
Next Time
